        "--prompt-en",
        "An environmental dark fantasy photograph of an adult fictional woman; her presence anchors a complex dark fantasy scene where magic has visible physical consequences. Use the supplied photograph for the woman's visible face and hair impression: a chin-length dark bob with a wispy fringe, large dark eyes, a softly rounded face tapering at the jaw, and softly full natural lips. She is a sluice keeper inside an abandoned abbey beneath a salt marsh. Her practical living armour is formed from overlapping dark seed-husk plates, with amber vascular tissue visible at their flexible seams. A thick living root valve spans a waist-high masonry sluice doorway. One continuous ribbed organic lining follows its exposed stone arch and right jamb, folding without a break into a flexible tissue hinge at the doorway edge beside the split root. The complete small doorway, the unbroken lining and its folded hinge remain exposed beside her hands. Black tidal water presses through a split in its bark toward a raised stone sill holding a small tray of pale seedlings. At the shutter she is grafting one of her armour's living scutes onto the split root. Her left palm supports the scute's lower rim while her right thumb and fingertips pinch its upper rim, leaving the central amber face and its contact with the bark exposed. Both elbows bend naturally below her shoulders, the repair is at her waist, and her forearms reach a short distance into the clear space on her right. A single flexible pale root cord runs continuously from her left forearm bracer to the scute. Fine amber capillaries spread from the scute across the torn bark, joining the armour organism to the gate root; the leak now escapes as a narrow silver thread. A wide fresh splash fan on the stone beneath it and the black pool rising below the nursery sill make the danger tangible. The damp open seam on her bracer shows the material she has given up for the graft. She stands securely on a narrow wet causeway, her torso in a comfortable quarter-turn, her eyes attending to the graft, her mouth slightly parted around a held breath. Her quiet concentration and the softness of her face remain the human center of the scene. Show her from mid-thigh upward, on the left of a horizontal frame, with her face, bracer, complete connecting cord, both hands, scute and bark contact visible together across the middle plane. The seedling sill sits behind the repair within the same readable space. Cold daylight filters down a narrow opening in the ribbed stone vault; the living amber tissue gives a restrained warm reflection to her fingers and cheek. Photograph the wet stone, fibrous bark, flexible plates and skin with tactile natural detail, at eye level through a normal lens, with sufficient depth to preserve the connection and its consequence.",
